 ZumaDash – Accomplished Master Plan  
 As built through Steps 1–5 + earlier core work
 Platform name: ZumaDash (Zuma Rock / Northern Abuja identity)  
 Service area only: Dutse · Kubwa · Bwari  

  1. Core product identity
- Hyper-local delivery marketplace (not a general Bolt clone)
- Hybrid app: light web (Node + React + MongoDB) + heavy WhatsApp tracking
- Uploads: Cloudinary  
- Email: bird.com 
- WhatsApp: Bird API (templates + free-form fallback)  
- Auth: JWT + roles Customer / Rider / Admin  
- Commission model: rider collects full agreed price → remits platform % by bank transfer  
- Bargaining + suggested price bands  
- Payment: Cash on Delivery + Bank Transfer (admin-editable account details + confirmation before booking)  
- Rich text/landmark addresses (GPS optional; photos + WhatsApp status when GPS is weak)  


  2. Public / marketing pages
- Landing page (sections + asset images: hero, how-it-works, why local, individual rider, fleet, trust, CTA)
- How It Works (`/how-it-works`)
- For Riders – Individual + Fleet (`/for-riders`)
- Pricing & Areas (`/pricing`) – same / neighbouring / cross-zone bands
- Terms – Customers (`/terms-customers`)
- Terms – Riders (`/terms-riders`)
- Legacy combined Terms (`/terms`)
- Navbar + footer links wired  


  3. Auth & accounts
- Register / Login  
- Guest booking → localStorage pending booking → auto-create job after signup/login  
- Role-based dashboards  
- Rider application (`/become-a-rider`) with NIN, bike details, guarantor  
- Admin must approve rider before rider dashboard access  
- Profile: name, phone; email display  
- Forgot-password path exists in email plan (hook points in notify)  


  4. Customer features
- Book delivery multi-step flow (pickup/drop-off text + photos, package size, suggested price, payment method)
- Bank transfer step: shows admin bank details (account name, number, bank name, amount) → user must confirm before booking  
- Saved addresses: add / delete / reuse on booking (tap once pickup, again drop-off)  
- My Deliveries with filters (All / Active / Completed / Cancelled–Dispute)  
- Track delivery page with status timeline + photo proofs  
- In-app notifications  
- Support tickets (chat with admin)  
- Push notifications (opt-in from Profile + auto after login when VAPID set)  


  5. Rider features
- Available jobs list + make / counter offers  
- Accept flow → agreed price → commission split stored  
- Status updates: LIVE → PICKED → DELIVERED with required photo proof where designed  
- Earnings page + commission owed / paid  
- Job history (`/rider/history`)  
- Profile: bike details update after approval  
- Push for new jobs / offer accepted  
- WhatsApp alerts (template-first)  


  6. Admin features (full control)
- Overview stats  
- Riders: list, approve/reject, freeze/unfreeze, commission mark-paid  
- Customers: list, freeze/unfreeze  
- Jobs: list, freeze, open dispute  
- Disputes: resolve → pay rider / customer side / partial  
- Finance: totals (owed / collected / rider net) + mark commission paid  
- In-app Notify: all customers or all riders  
- Email Centre: templates CRUD + send to all customers/riders  
- Reports: 7/30/90 days – jobs by status, revenue, est. commission, new users, finance  
- Settings: platform name, logo upload (Cloudinary) or URL, bank details, commission %, editable price bands  
- Support ticket control (admin side of chat)  


  7. Tracking & safety (anti-fraud design)
- WhatsApp-first status (LIVE / PICKED / DONE) when GPS is unreliable  
- Photo proof on key status changes  
- Disputes freeze job/earnings until admin resolves  
- Mutual evidence (photos, timestamps, trust score fields)  
- Account freeze for customers or riders  
- Progressive penalties path via admin tools  


 8. Money model (implemented)
- Agreed price after bargaining/offers  
- Rider collects full amount (COD or customer bank-transfer confirm)  
- Platform commission % of agreed price → `commissionOwed` on rider  
- Admin marks commission paid when rider remits by bank transfer  
- No physical office required for settlement  


  9. Notifications stack
- In-app Notification model + list UI  
- Email events: booking, status, freeze, support, commission, rider application  
- WhatsApp: Bird free-form + approved templates (`WA_TEMPLATE_NEW_JOB`, `WA_TEMPLATE_STATUS`, `WA_TEMPLATE_OFFER`)  
- Web Push (VAPID): logo icon/badge, deep link URL; service worker `sw.js`  


  10. Technical foundation (as built)
- Frontend: React (mobile-first), React Router, AuthContext  
- Backend: Node.js + Express  
- Database: MongoDB (Users, Jobs, Notifications, SupportTickets, PlatformSettings, EmailTemplates)  
- File uploads: Cloudinary (single/multi + guest base64 path for pending booking)  
- Real-time: Socket.io mounted (chat/status ready)  
- Env-driven: Mongo, JWT, Cloudinary, Bird, VAPID, WhatsApp template slugs, platform name/logo  


 11. Explicitly completed “remaining steps” blocks
1. Admin customers / disputes / notify / finance  
2. Full public marketing pages  
3. Profiles, saved addresses, My Deliveries, rider history/docs  
4. Email Centre, logo + price bands settings, reports  
5. Browser push + WhatsApp template hooks  


 12. Ops still required outside code (not “missing features”)
- Bird WhatsApp template approval in Bird dashboard  
- Generate and set VAPID keys (`npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`)  
- Production HTTPS (required for push)  
- Real MongoDB / Cloudinary / Bird credentials in `.env`  
- Optional: Firebase if you prefer FCM over pure Web Push  


  13. How to use this document later
Paste this whole block into a new chat and say e.g.:  
- “Expand ZumaDash from this accomplished master plan: add [feature]”  
- “Audit this plan against the codebase and implement gaps”  
- “Add Phase: fleet multi-rider assignment / invoice PDFs / map zones”  

 Single source of truth for what is already built: this document + the latest zip.




 //features to be built now

 PART 0 – What is already built (do not rebuild)

Use this as the base. All NOW work extends it; do not replace these behaviours.

- Hyper-local only: Dutse · Kubwa · Bwari  
- Roles: Customer, Rider, Admin (Merchant is added in NOW-8)  
- Book flow, guest pending booking, COD + bank transfer details display  
- Bargaining / offers, suggested zone price bands  
- WhatsApp + photo status tracking, Cloudinary uploads  
- Rider apply (individual), admin approve before rider dashboard  
- Commission owed, admin mark paid, freeze, disputes  
- Support tickets, in-app notify, email hooks, web push hooks  
- Admin: users, jobs, finance, email centre, reports, settings (bank, logo, bands, commission %)  
- Profile, saved addresses, my deliveries, rider history/earnings  

 How money and jobs already interact (unchanged spine):
Customer books → riders see job when status allows → offers/agree price → rider runs LIVE → PICKED → DELIVERED → platform commission tracked on rider → admin tools for freeze/dispute.  

NOW features insert gates on that spine (payment approval before riders see job; clearance before earnings are withdrawable) and add merchant, media, profile photo, counter-offer UX, rider public page, and track lightbox—without removing bargaining, WhatsApp tracking, or zone bands.


  PART 1 – IMPLEMENT NOW (full set)

These fix trust, money, fleet control, offers UX, and media viewing.


 NOW-1 – Bank transfer payment gate (before riders see the job)

 Why now: Stops fake “I paid” bookings and protects riders.

 Process
1. Customer books and chooses Bank Transfer.  
2. App shows platform bank details: account name, account number, bank name, amount to pay (from suggested/agreed flow amount at booking).  
3. Customer confirms “I have transferred” → job status = `pending_payment_approval`.  
4. While in `pending_payment_approval`, job is not returned by available-jobs APIs and riders are not notified.  
5. Admin Payment desk lists pending transfers: job id, customer, amount, time, optional customer reference note.  
6. Admin Approve → status becomes `pending_offers` → notify eligible riders (in-app + WhatsApp + push).  
7. Admin Reject → customer notified; job cancelled or returned so customer can pay again or switch to COD.  
8. COD jobs skip this gate → status goes straight to `pending_offers` and riders are notified.

Works with: NOW-14 (queue), NOW-15 (offers only after `pending_offers`), existing bank details in Platform Settings.

Build notes: Extend job status enum; filter `GET available jobs` to exclude `pending_payment_approval`; Payment desk approve/reject endpoints.


 NOW-2 – Completion clearance gate (rider earning not auto-withdrawable)

Why now: Stops fake “delivered” from inflating balances.

Process
1. Rider marks Delivered/Completed and must supply photo and/or video proof (and any existing status media rules).  
2. Job status → `pending_clearance`.  
3. Rider’s share for that job is posted to pending clearance, not to available balance.  
4. Admin opens job timeline + proofs (NOW-5, NOW-16) → Approve completion → amount moves from pending clearance to that rider’s available balance; job can move to `completed`.  
5. Admin may open dispute or reject clearance → amount stays frozen/pending; job stays non-withdrawable for that earning.  
6. Rider dashboard always shows three separate figures: Pending clearance · Available · Commission owed.

Works with: NOW-3 (withdraw only from available), NOW-4 (commission), NOW-9 merchant flags, NOW-11 merchant withdraw from rider available only.

Build notes: Never add a delivered job’s rider earning straight into withdrawable balance in one step.


  NOW-3 – Rider bank KYC + withdraw page

 Why now: Needed before any real payouts.

 Process – bank details
1. Rider opens bank details form: bank name, account name, account number.  
2. Submit → status `submitted`.  
3. Admin verifies → `approved` or `rejected` (rejection includes reason; rider can resubmit).  
4. Only an approved bank account may be used as destination for withdrawals.

 Process – withdraw
1. Rider requests a withdraw amount ≤ available balance (not pending clearance).  
2. System blocks if `commissionOwed > 0`, or if this rider is merchant-managed and Block rider withdrawals is on (NOW-9).  
3. Admin pays outside the app, then marks the withdraw request Paid (optional payment reference).  
4. Rider receives in-app notification + email with amount and outcome.

 Works with: NOW-2 (available balance), NOW-4 (commission block), NOW-11 (merchant path uses same available balance rules).


 NOW-4 – Admin settle commission (one job / settle all)

Why now: Matches “no physical office” collection.

 Process
1. Rider remits platform commission by bank transfer (off-platform or with a reference note the admin can see).  
2. Admin opens that rider’s finance view → Settle on one commission line (one job) or Settle all for that rider.  
3. `commissionOwed` is reduced or cleared; a settlement record is stored (who, when, amount, optional note).  
4. When `commissionOwed` becomes 0, withdraw is no longer blocked by the commission rule (NOW-3).

 Works with: NOW-3, NOW-14 (commission settlements in Payment desk), NOW-10 (merchant sees sum of riders’ commission owed).


 NOW-5 – Admin job timeline (exact timestamps)

 Why now: Disputes and clearance depend on it.

 Process
1. Every status change appends to `statusHistory` with: exact timestamp, actor user id, status label, optional note, optional media urls.  
2. Typical sequence rows include: Created, Payment approved (or COD skip), Offer accepted, LIVE, PICKED, DELIVERED, Pending clearance, Cleared/Completed, Disputed, Cancelled, etc.  
3. Admin job detail page shows this list in chronological order.  
4. Each row that has media is clickable to open that media (same lightbox behaviour as NOW-16 where applicable).

 Works with: NOW-1, NOW-2, NOW-14, disputes, NOW-15 offer accept time.


 NOW-6 – Admin view full user/rider/merchant docs and media

Why now: Safe approval of individuals and fleets.

 Process
1. Admin opens Riders or Merchants → opens one profile.  
2. Admin sees: contact fields, NIN, guarantor, verification status, freeze status, bike list (for merchant: each bike), images, playable videos, documents.  
3. Admin Approve, Reject, or Request re-upload (with note).  
4. Same document viewer is used for individual rider apply (NOW-7) and merchant fleet apply (NOW-8).


  NOW-7 – Individual rider apply: bike photos, video, documents

 Why now: Small change, big trust.

 Process
1. Applicant chooses Individual.  
2. Existing fields remain (identity, NIN, guarantor, bike plate/model/colour as already designed).  
3. Additional required/optional as you set: upload bike documents; upload bike photos; optional one bike video.  
4. Submit → `role: rider`, `verificationStatus: under_review`.  
5. Admin uses NOW-6 to view media → approve/reject.  
6. Only when approved does login route to the rider dashboard and allow taking jobs (subject to any later merchant flags if not independent).

  NOW-8 – Merchant (fleet) role – application

 Why now: Foundation for fleet control.

 Process
1. Applicant chooses Fleet on apply.  
2. Field Number of bikes (integer N ≥ 1) is shown.  
3. For each bike `1 … N` (repeatable sections, expand or “+”): bike name/label, plate number, photos, video, documents for that bike.  
4. Owner-level fields remain (NIN, guarantor, etc.).  
5. Successful submit → user `role: merchant` (not `rider`), `verificationStatus: under_review`.  
6. Admin reviews all bikes’ images/videos/documents (NOW-6) → approve or reject.  
7. When approved, login redirects to Merchant dashboard, not rider dashboard.  
8. On approval, system creates Bike records linked to that merchant from the submitted bike list (feeds NOW-9).


  NOW-9 – Merchant: bikes + create riders + control flags

 Why now: Without this, merchant is only a label.

 Process – bikes
1. After merchant approval, Bike records exist for that merchant.  
2. Merchant dashboard lists approved bikes (adding more bikes after approval is later phase; not required in this NOW set).  
3. Only approved bikes appear in “select bike” when creating a rider.

 Process – create rider
1. Merchant goes to Add rider.  
2. Fields: email, password, select bike (approved bikes only), plate number read-only and filled when bike is selected.  
3. Toggles (merchant-only; stored on rider):  
   - Allow rider to take jobs  
   - Suspend rider  
   - Block rider withdrawals  
   - Allow merchant to withdraw from this rider’s cleared (available) balance  
4. Submit → create user `role: rider`, linked `merchantId`, `bikeId`, flags set as chosen.  
5. Platform emails the rider: account created, login email/password, and what they can or cannot do under merchant settings.  
6. Rider logs in → rider dashboard. Server enforces flags on job accept and withdraw. Rider may edit personal info (name, phone, profile photo) only—not merchant toggles.

 Process – all riders page
1. Merchant sees all riders under their account.  
2. Click a rider → personal summary + all toggles + Save (effects apply immediately on server).  
3. Delete with confirmation. Rule: block delete if the rider has an active job (`accepted`, `live`, `picked`, or `pending_clearance`); merchant must wait until job is completed, cancelled, or cleared. No silent delete of in-flight delivery accounts.

 Works with: NOW-2/3 (withdraw), NOW-15 (allow take jobs), NOW-11, NOW-17 (fleet vs independent on public profile).

  NOW-10 – Merchant dashboard stats + history

 Why now: Merchants need operational visibility.

 Process
1. Dashboard stats (for this merchant’s riders only):  
   - Total deliveries completed  
   - Total not completed (active / cancelled / disputed as defined in filters)  
   - Total commission owed (sum of those riders’ `commissionOwed`)  
   - Total earnings of those riders (show pending clearance vs available if both exist)  
2. Filters: optional one rider + period (today, one week, one month, one year).  
3. Some stats as charts (e.g. deliveries over time, earnings over time); some as plain numbers.  
4. History page: all delivery rows across the fleet with the same rider + period filters (job id, rider, status, amounts, timestamps).


  NOW-11 – Merchant withdraw from rider (if allowed)

 Why now: Fleet cash control with strict rules.

 Process
1. Merchant opens Withdraw, selects one of their riders.  
2. Allowed only if:  
   - Toggle  Allow merchant to withdraw from this rider’s account is on, and  
   - Rider has available balance &gt; 0, and  
   - Commission block rule is satisfied (same as NOW-3: typically `commissionOwed === 0` unless you explicitly allow merchant withdraw while commission is owed—default is block if commission owed).  
3. Merchant requests payout amount ≤ that rider’s available balance → funds leave rider available balance; payout destination is merchant’s admin-approved bank account (merchant must complete same bank KYC pattern as riders, approved by admin).  
4. Rider receives in-app notification + email with amount and time.  
5. If the toggle is off → API and UI block the action.


 NOW-12 – Merchant support + notifications

Why now: Closes the fleet ops loop.

 Process – support
1. Merchant opens Support and selects recipient type:  
   - Support → conversation goes to admin  
   - All riders → message goes to every rider under this merchant  
   - One rider → message goes to that rider only  
2. Threads support send and reply for both sides as in existing support chat behaviour.  
3. Merchant may close tickets/threads with their riders.  
4. Merchant may not close tickets with admin; only admin closes admin-side support tickets.

 Process – notifications
1. Merchant receives in-app (and email where configured) events about their riders: offer accepted, delivered, pending clearance, dispute, withdraw, etc.  
2. Daily summary: email + in-app digest of that day’s deliveries and statuses across the fleet.


 NOW-13 – Voice note + video on booking (optional fields)

 Why now: Helps non-map addresses; Cloudinary already available.

 Process
1. Booking form includes optional voice note (audio), optional short video, plus existing photos.  
2. Files upload to Cloudinary; URLs stored on the job (pickup/drop/booking media fields as appropriate).  
3. Visible to assigned/offering riders and to admin.  
4. Not required to submit a booking (avoids blocking users on poor networks).  
5. On track page, these media are usable under NOW-16 (play voice, lightbox for video/photos).


  NOW-14 – Admin “Payment desk” single queue

 Why now: One daily workflow for money.

 Process
1. Admin Payment desk uses tabs or filters:  
   - Pending bank transfers (NOW-1)  
   - Pending completion clearances (NOW-2)  
   - Withdraw requests (NOW-3 and merchant-initiated NOW-11)  
   - Commission settlements (NOW-4)  
2. Each row shows enough context (job/rider/customer, amount, time) to Approve / Reject / Settle in one or two clicks.  
3. Actions call the same rules as NOW-1–4 and NOW-11; desk is the UI shell, not a second set of money rules.


  NOW-15 – Offers, counter-offers, and rider notifications (marketplace loop)
 
Why now: Completes booking after payment gate; keeps bargaining as the price mechanism.

 Process
1. When job reaches `pending_offers` (COD immediately after create, or after NOW-1 admin approve for bank transfer), eligible riders receive notifications (in-app + push + WhatsApp as already wired).  
2. Rider opens available job → submits an offer (price + optional short note).  
3. Customer sees all open offers for that job.  
4. For each offer, customer may:  
   - Accept → that price becomes agreed price; job → `accepted`; other offers closed; rider notified; commission fields calculated from agreed price; or  
   - Counter-offer a new price on that offer.  
5. Rider is notified of counter-offer and may Accept counter, Counter again, or Decline.  
6. Ping-pong continues until one side accepts or the offer is declined/expired by your existing rules.  
7. After job is `accepted`, no new offers are accepted on that job.  
8. Merchant flag Allow rider to take jobs / Suspend (NOW-9): if off/suspended, that rider does not receive the job in available list and cannot submit offers.

 Works with: NOW-1 (when notifications fire), NOW-17 (name on offer), existing zone suggested price (suggestion only).


  NOW-16 – Profile pictures (customer and rider)

 Why now: Needed for offer cards and rider public page.

 Process
1. Customer and rider open Profile → upload or change profile picture.  
2. Image goes to Cloudinary; `profilePhoto` saved on the user.  
3. Merchant-created riders may set their own profile photo as personal info.  
4. Photo is shown on: own profile, offer list thumbnails, rider public details page (NOW-17), admin user detail.  
5. If no photo, show a default avatar.


  NOW-17 – Clickable rider name on offers → rider public details page

 Why now: Trust before accepting an offer.

 Process
1. On the customer offer list (and on track page after assignment, on the assigned rider name), the rider display name is a link.  
2. Link opens Rider public details page for that rider.  
3. Page displays only:  
   - Profile photo  
   - Name  
   - Mobile number  
   - Rating  
   - Number of completed jobs  
   - Date joined  
   - Type: Independent rider or Fleet rider (fleet if `merchantId` is set; otherwise independent)  
4. Page does not show: NIN, guarantor, documents, bank details, commission owed, merchant control toggles.  
5. Access policy for this NOW set: customer may open this page from a job where that rider has placed an offer or is assigned (not a global public directory).  
6. User returns to the offer list or track page without losing job context.


 NOW-18 – Track page media lightbox + voice playback

Why now: Both sides need clear proof without leaving the page.

 Process
1. On the tracking page, pickup photos, drop-off photos, booking photos, status-proof photos, and any video appear as thumbnails (or inline players where appropriate).  
2. Either customer or rider (or admin viewing the same job) clicks a photo or video → full-size lightbox overlay on the same page.  
3. Video plays inside the lightbox.  
4. User closes via control or backdrop click → overlay closes; media return to normal thumbnail size; user remains on the tracking page.  
5. If a voice note exists on the job, both customer and rider see a play/pause control and can listen without leaving the page.  
6. Same lightbox pattern is available to admin when opening media from the job timeline (NOW-5).

 Works with: NOW-13 (booking voice/video), status photo proofs already in the product.


 PART 2 – How all NOW features work together (single spine)

1.  Apply  
   - Individual → NOW-7 media → admin NOW-6 → approved rider.  
   - Fleet → NOW-8 → admin NOW-6 → approved merchant → bikes exist → NOW-9 create riders with flags.

2.  Profile  
   - Customer/rider set photo (NOW-16). Rider may set bank KYC (NOW-3). Merchant sets merchant bank KYC before NOW-11.

3.  Book 
   - Optional voice/video/photos (NOW-13).  
   - COD → `pending_offers`.  
   - Bank transfer → confirm paid → `pending_payment_approval` → admin Payment desk (NOW-1, NOW-14) → `pending_offers`.

4.  Match
   - Riders notified (NOW-15), subject to merchant allow/suspend flags.  
   - Offers + counter-offers until accept (NOW-15).  
   - Customer opens rider name → public profile photo, phone, rating, completed count, joined, independent/fleet (NOW-17).

5.  Execute  
   - Track page: status + lightbox media + voice play (NOW-18).  
   - Timeline logged for admin (NOW-5).

6.  Complete & money 
   - Rider marks delivered + proof → `pending_clearance` (NOW-2).  
   - Admin clears on Payment desk → available balance.  
   - Commission owed until admin settles one/all (NOW-4).  
   - Rider withdraw to approved bank if available and not blocked (NOW-3).  
   - Merchant may withdraw from rider available only if toggle on (NOW-11).  
   - Merchant sees stats/history (NOW-10), support and daily summary (NOW-12).


  PART 3 – Job status values this NOW set relies on

Use these consistently (extend existing enum; do not invent parallel silent states):

- `pending_payment_approval` — bank transfer waiting admin  
- `pending_offers` — visible to riders for offers  
- `accepted` — price agreed, rider assigned  
- `live` / `picked` / `delivered` — execution (existing names kept)  
- `pending_clearance` — delivered, earning not yet available  
- `completed` — admin cleared completion  
- `cancelled` / `disputed` / `frozen` — existing handling remains  

COD: skip `pending_payment_approval`.  
Bank transfer: never notify riders before leaving `pending_payment_approval` via admin approve.


  PART 4 – Role login targets after this NOW set

| Role | When allowed into main app | Destination |
|------|----------------------------|-------------|
| Customer | Registered | Customer dashboard |
| Rider (independent) | Admin approved | Rider dashboard |
| Rider (fleet-created) | Created by merchant; flags apply | Rider dashboard |
| Merchant | Admin approved fleet application | Merchant dashboard |
| Admin | Admin account | Admin dashboard |



 PART 5 – Explicit non-changes in this NOW set

- Bargaining remains the way final price is set; suggested bands remain suggestions only.  
- WhatsApp + photo tracking remain primary where GPS is weak.  
- Service area remains Dutse · Kubwa · Bwari only.  
- Map per-km pricing and AI landmark pricing stay out of this NOW document (later roadmap).  
- Merchant cannot close admin support tickets.  
- Rider cannot edit merchant control flags.  
- Delete fleet rider blocked while they have an active job (rule fixed above).  





















