  PART 2 – IMPLEMENT LATER (solid, but after money + merchant)

 LATER-1 – Hybrid map (only when coordinates exist)

 Process
1. On book: user may drop pin / search place or use text+landmark only.  
2. If both pickup and drop have coordinates → store `mapDistanceKm`, show route on track page.  
3. If not → zero map dependency; WhatsApp + photos + text remain primary.  
4. Hard or soft block if pin is outside Dutse–Kubwa–Bwari polygon.


  LATER-2 – Admin ₦ per km + formula for suggested price

 Process
1. Settings: rate per km, minimum fare, optional size multipliers.  
2. When `mapDistanceKm` exists:  
   `suggested = max(minimum, distance × rate × sizeFactor)`  
3. Still only a suggestion; offers/bargaining unchanged.  
4. When no distance → existing zone bands.


  LATER-3 – AI / rules-assisted price for non-map jobs

 Process
1. Inputs: zone, package size, landmark text, optional user “estimated km”, history of similar jobs.  
2. Output: suggested range + one-line reason.  
3. Start **rules + averages; add ML only when volume exists.  
4. Admin on/off + min/max caps.


 LATER-4 – Landmark library

 Process
1. Save successful landmarks from jobs.  
2. Admin moderate.  
3. Autocomplete on book; feed LATER-3 pricing.


  LATER-5 – Proof pack standard

 Process
1. Prompt photo at pickup + drop (+ optional voice “handed over”).  
2. One bundle on track page; optional “share via WhatsApp”.  
3. Improves dispute outcomes more than GPS.


  LATER-6 – Trust badges on offers

 Process
1. Score from completion rate, disputes, photo compliance, commission behaviour.  
2. Simple badge on rider offer card for customers.  
3. Keep non-toxic (no public pile-on).


  LATER-7 – Delivery windows

 Process
1. Optional: morning / afternoon / evening.  
2. Rider sees window on job card.


  LATER-8 – Merchant add more bikes after approval

 Process
1. Merchant submits extra bike (media + plate) → admin approve → appears in “select bike” for new riders.


  LATER-9 – Full fleet assignment console

 Process
1. Which rider is on which job live.  
2. Reassign only if no active LIVE (or with rules).  
3. Don’t build until NOW merchant stats + riders work.


  LATER-10 – Offline draft booking for logged-in users

 Process
1. Auto-save form to localStorage.  
2. Resume banner on return (guest pending booking already exists).


  LATER-11 – Multi-language UI (e.g. Hausa + English)

 Process
1. Critical screens first: book, track, payment instructions, rider status buttons.


  LATER-12 – Automated accounting exports

Process
1. CSV of jobs, commissions, withdrawals per period for admin/merchant.


 PART 3 – Money state machines (copy into any build chat)

  Customer bank transfer
`created` → `pending_payment_approval` → (admin approve) → `pending_offers` → `accepted` → `live` → `picked` → `delivered` → `pending_clearance` → (admin approve) → `completed`

  Rider balances
- Pending clearance: delivered, not admin-cleared  
- Available: cleared, not withdrawn  
- Commission owed: platform share not settled  

  Withdraw rules (recommended defaults)
- Rider withdraw: available only; blocked if commission owed > 0 or merchant blocked withdrawals  
- Merchant withdraw from rider: only if toggle on + available + same commission policy you choose  

  Commission
On clear/complete: increase rider `commissionOwed` by platform % of agreed price  
Admin settle one / settle all → decrease owed  


  PART 4 – Role & login matrix

| Role | Created how | Login destination if approved |
|------|-------------|-------------------------------|
| Customer | Register | `/dashboard` |
| Rider (individual) | Apply individual | `/rider` |
| Rider (fleet) | Merchant creates | `/rider` (flags apply) |
| Merchant | Apply fleet | `/merchant` |
| Admin | Seeded / manual | `/admin` |

Unapproved merchant/rider → under-review screen, no ops dashboard.


 PART 5 – Recommended implementation sequence

 Sprint A (money trust)  
NOW-1, NOW-2, NOW-3, NOW-4, NOW-5, NOW-14  

 Sprint B (docs + individual media)
NOW-6, NOW-7, NOW-13  

Sprint C (merchant core)
NOW-8, NOW-9, NOW-10  

Sprint D (merchant money + comms)
NOW-11, NOW-12  

Sprint E (map + pricing intelligence) 
LATER-1, LATER-2, then LATER-3, LATER-4  

Sprint F (standout polish)
LATER-5, LATER-6, LATER-7, LATER-10


 PART 6 – Explicit non-goals (keep product sharp)

- National coverage  
- Removing bargaining  
- Forcing map for every address  
- Instant automatic bank payouts without admin  
- Rider editing merchant control flags  
- Merchant closing admin support tickets  
- Building full AI before you have job history volume  






//later feature been built NOW
 ZumaDash – Map Mode + Live Tracking + Suggested Price (Paste-Ready Master Plan) 
 Implement exactly as written. Do not invent alternate behaviour.

  1. Purpose

Add optional map mode for booking and tracking when both pickup and drop-off are pinned on the map.  
If the user does not use the map (or only one side is pinned), the app stays on the existing text/landmark path and existing zone price bands.

Live rider movement on the track page is required only for map-mode jobs.

Bargaining, offers, bank-transfer gate, clearance, WhatsApp, and photo proofs remain unchanged.

Service area only: Dutse · Kubwa · Bwari.


  2. Two location modes (mandatory on every job)

Every job must store:

- `locationMode: "map"` or `locationMode: "text"`

 Map mode is allowed only when:

- Pickup has valid `lat` + `lng`, and
- Drop-off has valid `lat` + `lng`, and
- Both pins are inside the Dutse–Kubwa–Bwari service area

 If only one coordinate exists, or either pin is missing, or either pin is outside the corridor:

- Job must be `locationMode: "text"`
- Map pricing, route map, and live tracking must not run
- User uses textareas / landmarks / photos / voice as already built

There is no half-map: one pin alone never enables map features.


  3. Booking behaviour

 UI

- User may either:
  - Use map: set both pickup and drop pins (search and/or drop pin), or
  - Use text: fill pickup and drop textareas only (existing flow)

 Rules

1. If user starts map and sets only one pin → do not allow submit as map mode; require the second pin or clear pins and use text.  
2. On submit with both valid in-corridor pins → `locationMode = "map"`, save both coordinates.  
3. On submit without both pins → `locationMode = "text"`, coordinates empty/ignored for map features.  
4. Optional media (photos, voice, video) work in both modes.

 Suggested price at booking

| Mode | How suggested price is calculated |
|------|-----------------------------------|
| `map` | Driving distance between the two pins → admin ₦/km formula (section 4) |
| `text` | **Existing zone bands only (same / neighbouring / cross × package size). No km formula. |

Suggested price pre-fills the price field. User may edit it.  
Final price is still set by offers / counter-offers / accept (existing NOW marketplace).  
Commission always uses agreed price, never suggested price alone.


 4. Map-mode price formula (admin-controlled)

 Admin settings (platform settings)

- `baseFare` (₦)  
- `ratePerKm` (₦ per km)  
- `includedKm` (km included in base; may be 0)  
- `minimumFare` (₦)  
- Size multipliers: `small`, `medium`, `large` (e.g. 1.0 / 1.15 / 1.35)

 Distance

- Use driving distance (Google Distance Matrix or Directions), not straight-line.  
- Store on job as `mapDistanceKm`.

 Formula (map mode only)

\[
\text{suggestedPrice} = \max\bigl(\text{minimumFare},\ \text{baseFare} + \text{ratePerKm} \times \max(0,\ \text{mapDistanceKm} - \text{includedKm}) \times \text{sizeFactor}\bigr)
\]

Text mode: do not call distance APIs; use existing zone band suggestion only.


 5. Tracking behaviour

 5.1 Text-mode jobs (`locationMode === "text"`)

- Existing status timeline (LIVE → PICKED → DELIVERED, etc.)  
- Photo / video lightbox and voice playback as already built  
- WhatsApp status updates as already built  
- No route map  
- No live rider marker  

  5.2 Map-mode jobs (`locationMode === "map"`)

Track page must show:

1. Map with:
   - Pickup pin  
   - Drop-off pin  
   - Route between them (from directions when available)  
2. Live rider movement while job is active:
   - When rider status is LIVE or PICKED, rider app/client sends current `lat`/`lng` on a short interval (e.g. every 3–5 seconds) to the backend  
   - Backend stores last known location for that job (optional short trail of recent points)  
   - Backend broadcasts updates over Socket.io (already in stack) to the customer (and rider) on the track page  
   - Customer track page updates the rider marker live without full page refresh  
3. Status timeline and photo proofs remain visible on the same page (GPS can still fail mid-trip; do not remove WhatsApp/photo process)  
4. Location streaming  stops when status becomes DELIVERED, cancelled, disputed, or completed  

If the rider device has no GPS fix temporarily, keep last marker position and rely on status + photos; do not break the track page.


 6. Rider client duties (map-mode jobs only)

1. After accepting a map-mode job, when rider taps LIVE (and while PICKED), start sharing geolocation to the server for that `jobId`.  
2. Stop sharing on DELIVERED / cancel / complete.  
3. Text-mode jobs: do not require or depend on location sharing for the product to work.


  7. Corridor (service area)

- Define a polygon/bounds for **Dutse · Kubwa · Bwari.  
- Any pin outside → reject for map mode (user must repin inside or switch to text mode).  
- Text-mode bookings remain limited by existing area rules/copy (still only this corridor as product policy).


  8. What does not change

- COD vs bank transfer payment gate  
- Offers / counter-offers / agreed price  
- Pending clearance / withdraw / commission  
- Merchant flags  
- WhatsApp + photo as safety net  
- Zone bands remain the suggestion engine for text mode



 9. Job fields to persist (minimum)

- `locationMode`: `"map"` | `"text"`  
- `pickup`: `{ description, lat?, lng?, photos?, ... }`  
- `dropoff`: `{ description, lat?, lng?, photos?, ... }`  
- `mapDistanceKm` (only when map mode)  
- `suggestedPrice`  
- `agreedPrice` (from offers, as now)  
- `riderLastLocation`: `{ lat, lng, updatedAt }` (map mode, while live)  
- Optional: `routePolyline` or encoded path for drawing  


 10. Implementation order (in this phase, all included)

1. Booking: both-pins-or-text rule + `locationMode`  
2. Corridor validation on pins  
3. Distance API + admin ₦/km settings + suggested price (map only; else zone bands)  
4. Track page: static map + route for map-mode jobs  
5. Live location: rider publish + Socket.io + moving marker on map-mode track page  

Implement all five do not ship map pricing without the both-pins rule; do not enable live tracking on text-mode jobs.



 11. Acceptance tests (must pass)

1. Text only booking → `locationMode = text` → suggested price from zone bands → track has no live map.  
2. One pin only → cannot submit as map mode.  
3. Two valid pins inside corridor → `locationMode = map` → `mapDistanceKm` set → suggested price from ₦/km formula.  
4. Pin outside corridor → blocked for map mode.  
5. Map-mode job, rider LIVE → customer track shows marker updating.  
6. Same job, rider DELIVERED → location updates stop.  
7. User still completes offers/bargain; agreed price overrides suggestion for commission.




Implement this document exactly: ZumaDash Map Mode + Live Tracking + Suggested Price Master Plan.

- Map mode ONLY when BOTH pickup and drop coordinates exist and are inside Dutse–Kubwa–Bwari.
- Otherwise text mode: existing textareas + existing zone band pricing + existing timeline tracking (no live map).
- Map mode suggested price = admin base + ₦/km × driving distance (and minimum/size factors). Text mode = zone bands only.
- Map-mode track page = map + route + LIVE rider movement via Socket.io; keep status/photo/WhatsApp as well.
- Do not remove bargaining, payment gates, or clearance flows.
- Extend the existing codebase; match existing auth, job, and notify patterns.



